      },
      "id": 21,
      "options": {
        "content": "### How to read this dashboard\n\n**Codex request** means a model turn Coditor saw, not every ChatGPT backend call.\n\n**Degraded session** means the session hit a problem Coditor can name, not just an early warning.\n\n**Degraded sessions %** is the main health number. Lower is better.\n\n**Degraded causes** tells you what kind of problem happened, so repeated patterns stand out.\n\n**Cached input %** shows how much Codex input came from provider cache reuse. Higher is usually better because less input had to be processed fresh.\n\n**Context fill** shows how much of the model context was used by input. Higher means less room is left.\n\n**Failed or incomplete responses** mean the Responses stream ended badly or stopped before a normal completion.\n\n**Model fallbacks** mean Codex asked for one model and got another.\n\n**Tool, skill, and MCP panels** only show events Coditor could see. Empty panels can mean telemetry is missing, not that nothing happened.\n\n**Estimated cost** is a best-effort cost estimate. It is useful for trends, but it may not match billing.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.1.0",
      "title": "Terminology Guide",
      "description": "Short definitions for the dashboard's main terms and KPIs.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
